Subject: Native compiler contracts of the original lesson and Challenge play units
Upstream-base: f75ccf1ad20e5bd7585962990db08067c0ae498a
Classification: native compiler contract; no game behavior change.

Retail MWCC emits header inline functions out of line, so units that see only
a declaration still link. GCC emits no out-of-line copy, which left the module
importing symbols nothing defines; lazy binding then aborted at the first call
(GetStrikerChallenge from the Challenge preview, seen at a 101 lesson start).

- OverlayHandlerChallengePreview.cpp includes the unchanged inline bodies of
  GetStrikerChallenge (GameInfo.inl), BaseSceneHandler::GetPresentation
  (BaseSceneHandler.inl) and the InlineHasher constructors (feInlineHasher.h).
- feButtonComponent.cpp includes the InlineHasher constructors as well; that
  shared frontend unit had the same latent import.

diff --git a/src/Game/FE/Overlay/OverlayHandlerChallengePreview.cpp b/src/Game/FE/Overlay/OverlayHandlerChallengePreview.cpp
--- a/src/Game/FE/Overlay/OverlayHandlerChallengePreview.cpp
+++ b/src/Game/FE/Overlay/OverlayHandlerChallengePreview.cpp
@@ -20,6 +20,13 @@
 #include "NL/nlLocalization.h"
 #include "NL/nlFormat_fwd.h"
 #include "NL/nlPrint.h"
+#if defined(MSCHARGED_NATIVE)
+// Retail emits these GameInfo, BaseSceneHandler and InlineHasher inlines out
+// of line in other units; natively this unit includes their unchanged bodies.
+#include "Game/BaseSceneHandler.inl"
+#include "Game/FE/feInlineHasher.h"
+#include "Game/GameInfo.inl"
+#endif
 
 #include <string.h>
 
